course: dictionary
lesson: 14082
title: Meddling and nosy neighbours
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When someone meddles, they get involved in things that are none of their business, and nobody asked them to. Look for clues in the sentence. «Mrs Pike is a meddling neighbour who reads everyone's letters.» The words who reads everyone's letters tell you that meddling means getting into other people's business.
explain: Meddling can be a noun, an adjective or a verb form. As a noun, it names the act: «Her meddling made the argument worse.» As an adjective, it describes a person: «a meddling neighbour». As a verb, it is the -ing form of meddle: «Stop meddling with my model!»
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. Does «Stop getting involved in my model, Sam!» still make sense? Yes, so meddling means getting involved when you are not wanted.
fact: Meddling means getting involved in other people's business when you are not wanted.
fact: «Meddling» can be a noun, an adjective or a verb form, and the meaning stays the same.
fact: «A meddling busybody» is someone who keeps interfering in other people's affairs.
fact: In the news, «foreign meddling» means one country interfering in another country's politics.
fact: Adults often say «Stop meddling!» to children who are fiddling with things they should leave alone.
exercise: «Mrs Pike is a meddling neighbour who reads everyone's letters.» What does meddling mean here? | *Getting involved in other people's business when not wanted | Moving house to the countryside | Singing loudly in the park | Cooking sweet treats for the whole street
exercise: «Stop meddling with my model!» What is Sam being asked to do? | Build a bigger model | *Keep his hands off and stop interfering | Hand the model to his teacher | Paint it in bright colours
exercise: «The meddling dog kept taking the children's sandwiches.» Find and copy one word that means interfering. | dog | children | *meddling | sandwiches
test: In the news, «foreign meddling» means: | A map showing where countries are | *One country interfering in another country's politics | Two countries sharing a sports team | A foreign holiday with lots of food
test: In «Stop meddling!», what kind of word is meddling? | *A verb form, the -ing form of meddle | An adjective describing a person | A noun for a thing | A name for a place
exam: Which sentence uses «meddling» as an adjective? | «The dog wagged its tail at the park.» | «Her meddling made the problem bigger.» | «Stop meddling with the clock!» | *«The meddling neighbour knocked on the door again.»
